`query_json` returns a JSON array string. For a json-typed property, it embeds it as a nested JSON object. So if I do `query_json('select AuditEntry { action, entity_type, version, snapshot }')`, the result is a JSON array where each element has `snapshot` as a nested object (already parsed when I json.loads the whole thing). 

